\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 20\'d720 Car Audio Booth Execution for Nakamichi Car Audio at SEMA Show 2024\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 At SEMA Show 2024, Nakamichi Car Audio needed a 20\'d720 booth that could make compact electronics feel clear, premium, and easy to approach inside a visually noisy hall. Car audio products do not win attention by size alone. They need controlled lighting, clean product hierarchy, and enough open space for visitors to stop, compare, and ask questions without the booth feeling crowded or overbuilt. The goal was to create a product-first environment that felt calm and technically credible from multiple approach angles.\cb1 \
\cb4 Because this project was built for the SEMA show floor in Las Vegas, the booth also had to perform under real venue conditions: dense aisle traffic, product-security needs, fast move-in timing, and a layout that could stay readable while supporting both quick browsing and deeper conversations. That broader context is why this case naturally connects to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.circleexhibit.com/events/sema-show"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf5 \ul \ulc5 SEMA Show}}.\cb1 \
