\f0\b\fs44 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 \cb4 \strokec2 Compact electronics stand out when the booth removes visual noise instead of adding more\cb1 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf6 \cb4 \strokec6 For a car audio booth like this, the real challenge is not getting attention once. It is keeping the space readable long enough for visitors to understand what they are looking at. Smaller electronics are easy to bury under oversized graphics, crowded counters, or inconsistent lighting. What made this booth work was restraint: each zone had a clear job, product displays stayed visible without feeling exposed, and the perimeter invited people in without creating congestion.\cb1 \
\cb4 Small audio components depend on lighting and spacing to remain easy to compare. Our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.circleexhibit.com/"}}{\fldrslt \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf5 \ul \ulc5 Las Vegas booth builders}} kept interaction points at the edges of Nakamichi\'92s booth, where visitors could inspect the products while the interior remained available for conversation.\cb1 \
